<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qara Yusuf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1420">1420</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qara Yusuf was the leader of the Qara Qoyunlu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> confederation from 1388 to 1420. Driven out by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>, he returned after Timur's death, killed the Jalayirid sultan Ahmad in 1410 and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, making the Qara Qoyunlu the leading power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>. In 1409 he also ended Artuqid rule at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardin">Mardin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qara-yusuf.jpg" alt="Qara Yusuf" width="252" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 15th century artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qara_Yusuf_enthroned,_15th_century.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Qara Yusuf was the son of Qara Mahammad Töremish, who died in a rebellion led by Pir Hasan. When the Qara Qoyunlu elders met to choose a successor they considered his brother Khwaja Misr, but the more energetic Qara Yusuf prevailed. He allied briefly with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-yuluk-osman">Kara Osman</a> and crushed Pir Hasan's forces. Early in his rule the Qara Qoyunlu allied with the Jalayirid dynasty at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a>, and he was for a time captured and jailed at Suşehri until his aunt Tatar Hatun paid a ransom. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> conquered Baghdad in 1393, and in 1394 imprisoned Khwaja Misr and sent him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a>.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Career</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>'s renewed campaign of 1400 defeated both the Qara Qoyunlu and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalayirid-sultanate">Jalayirids</a>, and Qara Yusuf took refuge with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a> and then with the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ankara">Battle of Ankara</a> in 1402 he returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, quarrelled with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-jalayir">Sultan Ahmad Jalayir</a> and drove him from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>. Timurid forces defeated him in 1403 at the Battle of Algami Canal, and he was imprisoned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> by order of the Mamluk sultan. Timur's death in 1405 freed him. He defeated the Timurid Abu Bakr at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakhchivan">Nakhchivan</a> on 14 October 1406 and retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a>. On 20 April 1408 he won the Battle of Sardrud, where Miran Shah was killed.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>Qara Yusuf defeated Sultan Ahmad near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> on 30 August 1410, and Ahmad was executed the next day. He then crowned his young son Pirbudag as sultan in 1411 while ruling as regent, and in 1412 defeated the combined forces of Shirvan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> at the Battle of Chalagan. Pirbudag died in 1418. Qara Yusuf himself died on 17 November 1420, on his way to fight the Timurid Shahrukh, who had demanded his submission. Shahrukh's campaigns against his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-iskander">Qara Iskander</a> in 1420–21 and 1429 failed, but in 1434–35 he succeeded and installed Qara Yusuf's son Jahan Shah as his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Qara Yusuf” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…of Oudh came from a Shia Muslim Sayyid family of Nishapur in Persia, descended from Musa al-Kadhim, and also traced descent on the paternal line to the Kara Koyunlu through <b>Qara Yusuf</b>; they were renowned for their secularism and broad outlook, and promoted Shia as the state religion.</blockquote><a href="/empire/awadh-state">Awadh State · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>Then came Timur: in 1400 the Timurids defeated the Qara Qoyunlu and <b>Qara Yusuf</b> fled to the Mamluk Sultanate, where Sultan an-Nasir Faraj, unwilling to anger Timur, imprisoned him with the Jalayirid sultan Ahmad Jalayir.</blockquote><a href="/empire/qara-qoyunlu">Qara Qoyunlu · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Ibrahim I submitted to Timur in 1386 and, with Timurid support, held off the Golden Horde, but in 1412 he and his ally Constantine I of Georgia were defeated by <b>Qara Yusuf</b> of the Qara Qoyunlu, and Ibrahim was captured and later ransomed.</blockquote><a href="/empire/shirvanshah-state">Shirvanshah State · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The last Artuqids were displaced by the Qara Qoyunlu leader <b>Qara Yusuf</b> in 1409, and Mardin later passed to the Aq Qoyunlu and the Ottomans.</blockquote><a href="/state/artuqids-of-mardin">Artuqids of Mardin</a></li><li><blockquote>Ahmad returned but was killed by <b>Qara Yusuf</b> of the Qara Qoyunlu in 1410.</blockquote><a href="/state/jalayirids">Jalayirids</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Erciş, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>. Died in Ujan, in what is now <a href="/countries/armenia">Armenia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=39.03,43.36&amp;year=1410" aria-label="Erciş on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5624 764 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Qara Yusuf"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6074 1034h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6074 1034h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=39.03,43.36&amp;year=1410">What was here in 1410? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
